    <h2>FAQ</h2>

    <h3>Is Klaviyo better than Mailchimp for ecommerce?</h3>
    <p>Yes, Klaviyo is better for ecommerce because it was built specifically for Shopify, WooCommerce, and BigCommerce stores. Klaviyo syncs product data, order history, and browsing behavior in real time, which enables revenue-driving automations like abandoned cart, browse abandonment, post-purchase flows, and win-back campaigns. Mailchimp has ecommerce features but its data sync is slower and its automations are less granular. For a store doing over $100,000 per year in revenue, Klaviyo's deeper ecommerce integration typically generates 20 to 30 percent more email revenue than Mailchimp.</p>

    <h3>Which is cheaper, Mailchimp or Klaviyo?</h3>
    <p>Mailchimp is cheaper at the entry level. The Essentials plan starts at $13 per month for 500 contacts, with a free tier available for up to 250 contacts and 500 monthly sends. Klaviyo's email plan starts at $20 per month ($35 with SMS included), and a free plan covers up to 250 profiles. For small lists under 500 contacts, Mailchimp is significantly cheaper. For ecommerce lists above 1,000 contacts, Klaviyo's higher revenue per subscriber usually justifies the higher cost.</p>

    <h3>Which has better automation, Mailchimp or Klaviyo?</h3>
    <p>Klaviyo has better automation for revenue-focused email marketing. Its flow builder supports conditional splits based on real-time behavior, predictive analytics for send time, and dynamic content blocks that pull product recommendations. Mailchimp's Customer Journey builder is capable for basic automations like welcome series and abandoned cart, but it lacks the depth of Klaviyo's behavioral triggers and predictive features. For simple newsletters, Mailchimp is sufficient. For sophisticated revenue automation, Klaviyo is the stronger choice.</p>

    <h3>Can I migrate from Mailchimp to Klaviyo?</h3>
    <p>Yes, you can migrate from Mailchimp to Klaviyo. Klaviyo offers a free migration tool that imports contacts, subscriber preferences, and segments directly from Mailchimp. The process typically takes a few hours for lists under 50,000 contacts. You will need to rebuild your automations in Klaviyo's flow builder, because Mailchimp Customer Journeys do not map directly to Klaviyo flows. Many Klaviyo customers report that rebuilding automations with Klaviyo's deeper data produces significantly better revenue than the original Mailchimp setup.</p>

    <h3>Which has better deliverability, Mailchimp or Klaviyo?</h3>
    <p>Both platforms have strong deliverability, but Klaviyo has a slight edge for ecommerce senders. Klaviyo's deliverability is optimized for engaged subscriber lists because it syncs purchase data and suppresses unengaged contacts automatically. Mailchimp has good deliverability for newsletters and content emails but can struggle with ecommerce volume if lists are not cleaned regularly. Independent deliverability tests in 2026 place both platforms above industry average, with Klaviyo slightly ahead for transactional and behavioral emails.</p>

    <h3>Can I use Mailchimp and Klaviyo together?</h3>
    <p>It is not recommended to run both platforms for the same audience, because it creates duplicate sends, conflicting data, and compliance issues. A common approach is to use Klaviyo for ecommerce email and SMS automation tied to your store, and use Mailchimp for non-ecommerce newsletters like a company blog or event announcements. If you have both a store and a content audience, this split can work, but most businesses consolidate on one platform within the first six months to simplify operations and reduce cost.</p>

